    "reviews": [
      {
        "name": "places/ChIJLwHpVJ8BBDQRHbyBCn0AF04/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pkdGJITmtNMDlJZERaMFEwWjZRazVMWkcxaGMwRRAB",
        "relativePublishTimeDescription": "11 個月前",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": {
          "text": "點了一碗下午茶細何五餸麵，份量比正常的少的，湯的味道很好，蘿蔔很甜，油麵不會太軟身\n原來想點蒜洋麻辣撈粗，但當天沒有了，所以點了烏冬作麵底，餸方面選了魚蛋，魚肉春卷和何車水魷，全部餸味道都很好，特別是魚肉春卷，味道非常好，整體的份量不算多。\n飲品點了檸檬茶和抺茶鮮奶，飲品一般般，抺茶鮮奶點了少甜可惜來的是走甜，就是一般的牛奶加上抺茶粉。\n當天下午三點當左右，入座率八成，上餐時間不算快，可以接受的。\n如果再經過附近會再吃一次！\n\nI ordered a bowl of afternoon tea noodle with five small dishes, which was smaller in portion than usual. The soup tasted great, the radish was very sweet, and the oil noodles weren't too soft.\n\nI originally wanted to order garlic and spicy noodle but it was unavailable that day, so I chose udon as the noodle base. For the side dishes, I selected fish balls, fish meat spring rolls, and cuttlefish with a flavorful sauce. All the side dishes were very tasty, especially the fish meat spring rolls, which had an excellent flavor. The overall portion wasn’t very large.\n\nFor drinks, I ordered iced lemon tea and matcha fresh milk. The drinks were average, I ordered the matcha fresh milk with less sweetness, but it came no sweet, just regular milk with matcha powder.\n\nAround three in the afternoon, the restaurant was about 80% full. The serving time wasn't very fast, but it was acceptable.\n\nIf I'm in the area again, I would definitely eat here once more!",
          "languageCode": "zh-Hant"
        },
        "originalText": {
          "text": "點了一碗下午茶細何五餸麵，份量比正常的少的，湯的味道很好，蘿蔔很甜，油麵不會太軟身\n原來想點蒜洋麻辣撈粗，但當天沒有了，所以點了烏冬作麵底，餸方面選了魚蛋，魚肉春卷和何車水魷，全部餸味道都很好，特別是魚肉春卷，味道非常好，整體的份量不算多。\n飲品點了檸檬茶和抺茶鮮奶，飲品一般般，抺茶鮮奶點了少甜可惜來的是走甜，就是一般的牛奶加上抺茶粉。\n當天下午三點當左右，入座率八成，上餐時間不算快，可以接受的。\n如果再經過附近會再吃一次！\n\nI ordered a bowl of afternoon tea noodle with five small dishes, which was smaller in portion than usual. The soup tasted great, the radish was very sweet, and the oil noodles weren't too soft.\n\nI originally wanted to order garlic and spicy noodle but it was unavailable that day, so I chose udon as the noodle base. For the side dishes, I selected fish balls, fish meat spring rolls, and cuttlefish with a flavorful sauce. All the side dishes were very tasty, especially the fish meat spring rolls, which had an excellent flavor. The overall portion wasn’t very large.\n\nFor drinks, I ordered iced lemon tea and matcha fresh milk. The drinks were average, I ordered the matcha fresh milk with less sweetness, but it came no sweet, just regular milk with matcha powder.\n\nAround three in the afternoon, the restaurant was about 80% full. The serving time wasn't very fast, but it was acceptable.\n\nIf I'm in the area again, I would definitely eat here once more!",
          "languageCode": "zh-Hant"
        },
